-- title:
--   Uniform original unbounded-variation HJB expected-payoff inequality for bounded compact stopping times
-- statement:
--   For every actual right-continuous stopped clock sigma below the original ruin-or-n horizon, with exact discounted w of post-dividend risk plus Stieltjes cash payoff, measurable and integrable nonnegative a.e., show the original Levy Ito-Meyer/HJB supermartingale calculation yields an expectation at most w(x). This isolates the genuinely hard stochastic compensation and Gaussian-plus-jump source budget from stopping-time construction and Fatou convergence.
-- source:
--   Independent original-source expectation component of fa7052b1. The exact payoff and original model are unchanged. It will be imported by a formally checked conditional parent proof; proof must derive the HJB inequality from the actual source, not merely restate it.

